{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeNh76Bmcd4cTLF8T5Fg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the workflow at `.github/workflows/test.yml`. It hasn't run on GitHub yet, and as written it will fail until the repo has a `package.json` and a lockfile. I checked that the YAML parses.\n\n**When it runs:** on pushes to `main` and on every pull request.\n\n**What it does:**\n1. Checks out the code (`actions/checkout@v4`).\n2. Installs Node.js 24.x, the current LTS line, with `actions/setup-node@v4`, and caches npm downloads.\n3. Runs `npm ci` to install dependencies exactly as recorded in the lockfile.\n4. Runs `npm test`.\n\n**What the repo still needs:**\n- **A `package.json` with a `test` script** (for example `\"test\": \"node --test\"` or `\"test\": \"jest\"`). Without it, `npm test` fails.\n- **A `package-lock.json` committed.** Both `npm ci` and `cache: npm` need it. Run `npm install` once to create it.\n\n**Ways to change it:**\n- **Exact version:** set `node-version: '24.11.0'` to pin a specific release.\n- **Version from a file:** to keep the version in one place, replace `node-version` with `node-version-file: '.nvmrc'` and commit a `.nvmrc` file.\n- **Several versions:** to test more than one version, add a matrix under the job, `strategy: { matrix: { node-version: ['20.x', '22.x', '24.x'] } }`, and set `node-version: ${{ matrix.node-version }}`.\n- **Other package managers:** for Yarn or pnpm, change `cache:` and the install command to match.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Let me know if you want me to commit this, or to set up a `package.json` too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":198,"cache_read_input_tokens":17212,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":198},"output_tokens":574,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_